  "facts": [
    "The Col. Patrick O'Rorke Bridge, completed in 1990, spans the Genesee River in Rochester, New York, connecting the neighborhoods of Corn Hill and the South Wedge.",
    "Named after Colonel Patrick O'Rorke, a hero of the Civil War, the bridge honors his legacy and contributions to the Union Army during the Battle of Gettysburg.",
    "With a total length of 1,200 feet, the Col. Patrick O'Rorke Bridge features a striking design that enhances the scenic beauty of the surrounding area while facilitating vital transportation."
